Source: https://github.com/devfile/api/issues/1216

State: CLOSED

Labels: area/library, kind/user-story

Title: Provide Mock Interface for Git Operations on devfile/library

Description:
/kind user-story

## Which area this user story is related to?

<!--
    Uncomment appropriate `/area` lines, and delete the rest.
    For example, `> /area api` would simply become: `/area api`
-->

/area library


## User Story

As a client of devfile/library, I should be able to use mock implementation in devfile/library for the Git operations, either git CLI or a git API client.

For example, the git pkg https://github.com/devfile/library/tree/main/pkg/git provides various functions that either use git CLI or git API client. So the devfile/library should provide an interface implementation for these mock functions.

```
func NewGitClient() GitClient {
	return GitClient{}
}

func NewMockGitClient() MockGitClient {
	return MockGitClient{}
}

func (c GitClient) Clone() {}

func (c MockGitClient) Clone() {}

type GitFuncs interface {
	Clone()
}

type ParserArgs struct {
	 // Path is a relative or absolute devfile path.
	Path string
	...
	// Expose the Git Interface to able to use mock implementation.
	Git GitFuncs
	...
}

parserArgs := parser.ParserArgs{
	HTTPTimeout:                   &httpTimeout,
	Git: NewMockGitClient(), // Git: NewGitClient(),
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

<!--
    Decide which specific steps need to be completed, outline subtasks.
-->
- [ ] Expose the Interface as part of the `ParserArgs`
- [ ] Mock implementation for all Git Cli/API operations
- [ ] Switch local tests to mock implementation
